03d;0.0521), (<bold>C</bold>) Log<sub>10</sub> hazard ratio&#x0003d;0.0015&#x02013;0.1781 &#x000d7; log<sub>10</sub> odds ratio for progressive disease (<italic>P</italic>&#x0003c;0.0001, <italic>R</italic><sup>2</sup>&#x0003d;38&#x00025;, s.e.&#x0003d;0.0380), (<bold>D</bold>) Log<sub>10</sub> hazard ratio&#x0003d;0.0135&#x0002b;0.5082 &#x000d7; log<sub>10</sub> ratio of median time to progression (<italic>P</italic>&#x0003c;0.001, <italic>R</italic><sup>2</sup>&#x0003d;56&#x00025;, s.e.&#x0003d;0.0928). The size of the symbols is proportional to the inverse of the variance (the weight). For time to progression the size is proportional to the number of patients in the trial.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="93-6602858f1"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Selected characteristics of the trials used in the analysis</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><td>&#x000a0;</td><td>&#x000a0;</td><td>&#x000a0;</td><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Treatment arms<sup>a</sup></bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Trial (first author &#x00026; reference)</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Country</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Year of patient recruitment<sup>b</sup></bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Group 1</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Group 2</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>No. of patients randomised</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"